00:30:40,392 --> 00:30:44,700
WITNESS B: side. People pull in off the highway or off 140th.

443
00:30:44,700 --> 00:30:49,150
ATTORNEY: How many cars were parked there while you were waiting?

444
00:30:49,150 --> 00:30:55,830
WITNESS B: A couple. One or two. It wasn't busy. People would pull in, run in, and leave.

445
00:30:55,830 --> 00:31:02,130
ATTORNEY: Were there any vehicles parked between the store and the highway while you were outside?

446
00:31:02,130 --> 00:31:07,700
WITNESS B: Not that I remember. Not big ones. Maybe a car came and went.

447
00:31:07,700 --> 00:31:09,550
OPPOSING COUNSEL: Object to form.

448
00:31:09,550 --> 00:31:14,370
ATTORNEY: I'll move on. Is the shoulder of the eastbound lanes paved?

449
00:31:14,370 --> 00:31:20,310
WITNESS B: There's a paved strip along the edge and then grass. Then the store lot.

450
00:31:20,310 --> 00:31:25,870
ATTORNEY: Is there a speed limit sign anywhere near there that you know of?

451
00:31:25,870 --> 00:31:30,077
WITNESS B: There's one somewhere back up the road. I believe it's

452
00:31:30,077 --> 00:31:33,660
WITNESS B: sixty-five out there, but don't hold me to it.

453
00:31:33,660 --> 00:31:35,150
OPPOSING COUNSEL: Object. Foundation.

454
00:31:35,150 --> 00:31:38,490
ATTORNEY: You're not certain of the posted limit?

455
00:31:38,490 --> 00:31:44,420
WITNESS B: No, I'm not certain. That's just what I think it is from driving it.

456
00:31:44,420 --> 00:31:47,796
ATTORNEY: Let me go back to what you had with you that

