00:31:53,320 --> 00:31:57,600
WITNESS B: My purse, and a shopping bag. One of those plastic

459
00:31:57,600 --> 00:32:01,110
WITNESS B: bags from the store with my things in it.

460
00:32:01,110 --> 00:32:02,970
ATTORNEY: Just one bag?

461
00:32:02,970 --> 00:32:09,640
WITNESS B: Just the one. The birdseed was the heaviest thing. I had it all in one bag.

462
00:32:09,640 --> 00:32:12,980
ATTORNEY: Which hand were you holding it in?

463
00:32:12,980 --> 00:32:17,764
WITNESS B: I'd switch. It was heavy. I think I had it in my left

464
00:32:17,764 --> 00:32:23,000
WITNESS B: hand most of the time, with my purse on my right shoulder.

465
00:32:23,000 --> 00:32:27,080
ATTORNEY: Did you set the bag down at any point?

466
00:32:27,080 --> 00:32:33,351
WITNESS B: I might have, on and off. I don't remember exactly. When everything happened, I know

467
00:32:33,351 --> 00:32:38,950
WITNESS B: I still had it, because I remember it banging against my leg when I jumped.

468
00:32:38,950 --> 00:32:43,030
ATTORNEY: When you say you jumped, what do you mean?

469
00:32:43,030 --> 00:32:47,850
WITNESS B: From the noise. The crash. It made me jump. That's all.

470
00:32:47,850 --> 00:32:51,478
ATTORNEY: We'll come to the crash in detail later. Did

471
00:32:51,478 --> 00:32:55,270
ATTORNEY: you have a cell phone with you that afternoon?

472
00:32:55,270 --> 00:32:57,500
WITNESS B: Yes. In my purse.

473
00:32:57,500 --> 00:33:01,950
ATTORNEY: Were you using your phone while you were waiting outside?

474
00:33:01,950 --> 00:33:06,625
WITNESS B: Not right then. Earlier I'd read my sister's text, when I

475
00:33:06,625 --> 00:33:10,480
WITNESS B: first got there. After that it was in my purse.

476
00:33:10,480 --> 00:33:16,040
ATTORNEY: So in the minutes before the collision, were you looking at your phone?

477
00:33:16,040 --> 00:33:20,490
WITNESS B: No. It was in my purse. I wasn't on it.

478
00:33:20,490 --> 00:33:26,430
ATTORNEY: Were you talking to anyone on the phone in the minutes before the collision?

479
00:33:26,430 --> 00:33:30,140
WITNESS B: No. I called my sister after. Not before.

480
00:33:30,140 --> 00:33:34,590
ATTORNEY: Were you texting, reading, or doing anything with the phone?

481
00:33:34,590 --> 00:33:38,478
WITNESS B: No. I know people will say I was on my phone,

482
00:33:38,478 --> 00:33:43,490
WITNESS B: but I wasn't. I was just standing there watching the road.

483
00:33:43,490 --> 00:33:47,200
OPPOSING COUNSEL: Move to strike the last part as nonresponsive.

484
00:33:47,200 --> 00:33:50,910
ATTORNEY: Were you listening to anything? Earbuds, headphones, music?

485
00:33:50,910 --> 00:33:53,510
WITNESS B: No. Nothing in my ears.

486
00:33:53,510 --> 00:33:56,480
ATTORNEY: Were you wearing glasses that afternoon?

487
00:33:56,480 --> 00:34:01,670
WITNESS B: No. I only wear reading glasses, and those were in my purse.

488
00:34:01,670 --> 00:34:06,120
ATTORNEY: Do you need glasses to see things at a distance?

489
00:34:06,120 --> 00:34:12,060
WITNESS B: No. My distance vision is fine. I just need the readers for small print.

490
00:34:12,060 --> 00:34:14,280
ATTORNEY: Were you wearing sunglasses?

491
00:34:14,280 --> 00:34:18,360
WITNESS B: No. I didn't have sunglasses with me that day.

492
00:34:18,360 --> 00:34:23,180
ATTORNEY: Did the sun bother you at all while you were waiting?

493
00:34:23,180 --> 00:34:27,640
WITNESS B: No. It wasn't in my face. I could see fine.

494
00:34:27,640 --> 00:34:29,490
OPPOSING COUNSEL: Object to form.

495
00:34:29,490 --> 00:34:33,940
ATTORNEY: Were you wearing a hat or anything with a brim?

496
00:34:33,940 --> 00:34:37,280
WITNESS B: No hat. Just my hair pulled back.

497
00:34:37,280 --> 00:34:40,990
ATTORNEY: Was anyone with you while you were outside?

498
00:34:40,990 --> 00:34:43,590
WITNESS B: No. I was by myself.

499
00:34:43,590 --> 00:34:48,040
ATTORNEY: Were you talking with anyone in person while you waited?

500
00:34:48,040 --> 00:34:53,600
WITNESS B: Not really. A man said hello going into the store. That's about it.

501
00:34:53,600 --> 00:34:56,940
ATTORNEY: Do you know who that man was?

502
00:34:56,940 --> 00:35:01,020
WITNESS B: No. Never seen him before. Just somebody stopping in.

503
00:35:01,020 --> 00:35:04,730
ATTORNEY: Did you see where he went after that?

504
00:35:04,730 --> 00:35:09,920
WITNESS B: Inside. I don't know after that. I wasn't paying him any attention.

505
00:35:09,920 --> 00:35:14,000
ATTORNEY: While you were waiting, what were you doing, generally?

506
00:35:14,000 --> 00:35:19,049
WITNESS B: Just waiting. Watching the road, watching for my sister's car. She'd

507
00:35:19,049 --> 00:35:22,910
WITNESS B: be coming from the west, so I kept looking that way.

508
00:35:22,910 --> 00:35:26,990
ATTORNEY: Why would your sister be coming from the west?

509
00:35:26,990 --> 00:35:31,291
WITNESS B: Because she lives west of there. She'd come down the highway

510
00:35:31,291 --> 00:35:35,520
WITNESS B: over that hill, same as anybody coming from that direction.

511
00:35:35,520 --> 00:35:39,970
ATTORNEY: So you were watching westbound or eastbound traffic for her?

512
00:35:39,970 --> 00:35:44,790
WITNESS B: Eastbound. She'd be heading east toward me, coming down the hill.

513
00:35:44,790 --> 00:35:48,500
ATTORNEY: What kind of car does your sister drive?

514
00:35:48,500 --> 00:35:52,580
WITNESS B: A little silver hatchback. I was looking for that.

515
00:35:52,580 --> 00:35:58,150
ATTORNEY: Did you watch the cars that came over the hill while you waited?

516
00:35:58,150 --> 00:36:02,517
WITNESS B: Every one of them. Every time something came over

517
00:36:02,517 --> 00:36:05,190
WITNESS B: I'd look to see if it was her.

518
00:36:05,190 --> 00:36:07,050
OPPOSING COUNSEL: Object to form.

519
00:36:07,050 --> 00:36:13,720
ATTORNEY: Was there anything that afternoon, before the collision, that seemed unusual to you about the traffic?

520
00:36:13,720 --> 00:36:20,030
WITNESS B: No. It was just a normal afternoon. Cars going by. Nothing unusual until it happened.

521
00:36:20,030 --> 00:36:23,953
ATTORNEY: Did you notice any vehicles pulling into or out of

522
00:36:23,953 --> 00:36:28,190
ATTORNEY: the store lot in the few minutes before the collision?

523
00:36:28,190 --> 00:36:32,270
WITNESS B: I don't remember any right then. It was quiet.

524
00:36:32,270 --> 00:36:37,090
ATTORNEY: Did you notice anyone walking along the highway, or crossing it?

525
00:36:37,090 --> 00:36:38,950
WITNESS B: No. Nobody walking.

526
00:36:38,950 --> 00:36:41,170
ATTORNEY: Any bicycles or motorcycles?

527
00:36:41,170 --> 00:36:43,400
WITNESS B: Not that I remember.

528
00:36:43,400 --> 00:36:48,220
ATTORNEY: Any emergency vehicles, police cars, anything with lights, before the collision?

529
00:36:48,220 --> 00:36:52,300
WITNESS B: No. Not before. Afterward, yes, a lot of them.

530
00:36:52,300 --> 00:36:56,123
ATTORNEY: Let me ask one more general question about where you

531
00:36:56,123 --> 00:37:00,460
ATTORNEY: were. Throughout the time you were waiting, where were you?

532
00:37:00,460 --> 00:37:04,540
WITNESS B: Outside. Out front of the store. I've said that.

533
00:37:04,540 --> 00:37:09,942
ATTORNEY: You have. I'm just making sure the record is clear. Did you go

534
00:37:09,942 --> 00:37:14,560
ATTORNEY: around to the side or back of the store at any point?

535
00:37:14,560 --> 00:37:17,160
WITNESS B: No. I stayed out front.

536
00:37:17,160 --> 00:37:22,720
ATTORNEY: Did you walk out toward the highway at any point before the collision?

537
00:37:22,720 --> 00:37:25,690
WITNESS B: No. I stayed by the store.

538
00:37:25,690 --> 00:37:30,510
ATTORNEY: Did you cross 140th Court at any point before the collision?

539
00:37:30,510 --> 00:37:31,620
WITNESS B: No.

540
00:37:31,620 --> 00:37:36,450
ATTORNEY: Had you ever waited outside that store before, on another day?

541
00:37:36,450 --> 00:37:40,322
WITNESS B: A few times. When I've gotten rides. It's an

542
00:37:40,322 --> 00:37:43,490
WITNESS B: easy place for people to pick me up.

543
00:37:43,490 --> 00:37:49,060
ATTORNEY: So you were familiar with what the intersection looks like from the store?

544
00:37:49,060 --> 00:37:53,140
WITNESS B: Yes. I know what it looks like from there.

545
00:37:53,140 --> 00:37:58,330
ATTORNEY: Before May 7, had you ever seen a collision at that intersection?

546
00:37:58,330 --> 00:38:04,640
WITNESS B: No. Never. I'd heard people say it's a bad crossing, but I'd never seen anything.

547
00:38:04,640 --> 00:38:07,600
OPPOSING COUNSEL: Object. Move to strike as hearsay.

548
00:38:07,600 --> 00:38:11,647
ATTORNEY: I'll ask you just about what you saw yourself. Before

549
00:38:11,647 --> 00:38:15,770
ATTORNEY: that day, had you yourself seen any near misses there?

550
00:38:15,770 --> 00:38:20,220
WITNESS B: Not that I can remember. Nothing that stuck with me.

551
00:38:20,220 --> 00:38:23,443
ATTORNEY: All right. In the minutes leading up to the

552
00:38:23,443 --> 00:38:27,640
ATTORNEY: collision, about how long had you been standing outside?

553
00:38:27,640 --> 00:38:31,379
WITNESS B: Ten minutes. Maybe a little more. I'd finished shopping

554
00:38:31,379 --> 00:38:35,050
WITNESS B: at around twenty-five after, so ten or twelve minutes.

555
00:38:35,050 --> 00:38:38,020
ATTORNEY: And how are you estimating that?

556
00:38:38,020 --> 00:38:42,423
WITNESS B: From when I got there and how long I was inside.

557
00:38:42,423 --> 00:38:46,550
WITNESS B: I didn't look at a clock. It's my best guess.

558
00:38:46,550 --> 00:38:50,758
ATTORNEY: Understood. Did anything distract you in those minutes before? Any

559
00:38:50,758 --> 00:38:54,710
ATTORNEY: noise, anything that pulled your attention away from the road?

560
00:38:54,710 --> 00:38:56,570
OPPOSING COUNSEL: Object to form.

561
00:38:56,570 --> 00:39:02,500
WITNESS B: No. Nothing like that. I was just looking at the road for my sister.

562
00:39:02,500 --> 00:39:08,070
ATTORNEY: Were you hungry, tired, not feeling well, anything of that sort that day?

563
00:39:08,070 --> 00:39:12,033
WITNESS B: No. I felt fine. I'd had lunch. I was a little

564
00:39:12,033 --> 00:39:16,600
WITNESS B: tired from the week, but nothing out of the ordinary.

565
00:39:16,600 --> 00:39:22,160
ATTORNEY: Had you had anything to drink that day other than water or tea?

566
00:39:22,160 --> 00:39:25,130
WITNESS B: No. Tea and water. That's all.

567
00:39:25,130 --> 00:39:30,320
ATTORNEY: Were you taking any medication that affects your vision or your memory?

568
00:39:30,320 --> 00:39:32,550
WITNESS B: No. Nothing like that.

569
00:39:32,550 --> 00:39:37,889
ATTORNEY: Okay. I think that covers the background of the afternoon. Next I want to

570
00:39:37,889 --> 00:39:43,301
ATTORNEY: move to the traffic you saw coming from the west, beginning with the first

571
00:39:43,301 --> 00:39:48,932
ATTORNEY: time you noticed the car. Before I do, is there anything about the conditions

572
00:39:48,932 --> 00:39:53,320
ATTORNEY: or the road we've discussed that you want to add or correct?

573
00:39:53,320 --> 00:39:56,536
WITNESS B: No. I think I've said it. It was clear,

574
00:39:56,536 --> 00:40:00,000
WITNESS B: it was quiet, and I was out front waiting.

575
00:40:00,000 --> 00:40:04,111
ATTORNEY: Let's turn now to the car itself. You told me a few minutes

576
00:40:04,111 --> 00:40:08,850
ATTORNEY: ago that you were outside, out front of the store, when it happened.

577
00:40:08,850 --> 00:40:13,170
ATTORNEY: I want to take this slowly. When did you first notice the car?

578
00:40:13,170 --> 00:40:17,067
WITNESS B: When it came over the hill. Off to the west, to my

579
00:40:17,067 --> 00:40:21,510
WITNESS B: left if I'm facing the road. That's where I first saw it.

580
00:40:21,510 --> 00:40:25,214
ATTORNEY: The hill crest you described earlier, the one about

581
00:40:25,214 --> 00:40:27,610
ATTORNEY: a quarter mile or so to the west?

582
00:40:27,610 --> 00:40:33,070
WITNESS B: Yes. It comes over that rise and then it's sort of downhill toward the intersection.

583
00:40:33,070 --> 00:40:37,250
ATTORNEY: What was it about the car that made you notice it?

584
00:40:37,250 --> 00:40:42,565
WITNESS B: It was dark, and it was by itself. There wasn't anybody right behind it or

585
00:40:42,565 --> 00:40:47,520
WITNESS B: right in front of it. It just kind of stood out coming down the hill.

586
00:40:47,520 --> 00:40:50,410
ATTORNEY: Can you describe the car for me?

587
00:40:50,410 --> 00:40:54,638
WITNESS B: A dark car. A sedan, four doors I think. Low to the ground.

588
00:40:54,638 --> 00:40:59,080
WITNESS B: Black or a real dark color, I couldn't tell you exactly which.

589
00:40:59,080 --> 00:41:01,330
ATTORNEY: Which direction was it traveling?

590
00:41:01,330 --> 00:41:05,180
WITNESS B: East. Coming toward the intersection from the west, heading east.

591
00:41:05,180 --> 00:41:10,000
ATTORNEY: How well could you see the car as it came toward the intersection?

592
00:41:10,000 --> 00:41:15,223
WITNESS B: I had a clear view of the car the whole way in. I watched

593
00:41:15,223 --> 00:41:20,720
WITNESS B: it right up until the moment it hit. Nothing was in the way.

594
00:41:20,720 --> 00:41:22,560
OPPOSING COUNSEL: Object to form.

595
00:41:22,560 --> 00:41:28,480
ATTORNEY: You can go ahead. Is there anything you want to add to that answer?

596
00:41:28,480 --> 00:41:31,800
WITNESS B: No. That's what happened. I saw it.

597
00:41:31,800 --> 00:41:37,794
ATTORNEY: All right. Let me break that down a little. When you first saw it at the

598
00:41:37,794 --> 00:41:44,370
ATTORNEY: top of the hill, about how far away would you say it was from the intersection?

599
00:41:44,370 --> 00:41:48,153
WITNESS B: Far. I don't know in feet. It was up at

600
00:41:48,153 --> 00:41:52,130
WITNESS B: the top of the hill. However far that is.

601
00:41:52,130 --> 00:41:56,315
ATTORNEY: That's fine. I don't want you to guess. Would it

602
00:41:56,315 --> 00:41:59,890
ATTORNEY: be fair to say it was some distance away?

603
00:41:59,890 --> 00:42:03,210
WITNESS B: It was a good ways off, yes.

604
00:42:03,210 --> 00:42:08,020
ATTORNEY: And once you noticed it, did you keep looking at it?

605
00:42:08,020 --> 00:42:10,970
WITNESS B: Yes. I kept looking at it.

606
00:42:10,970 --> 00:42:14,300
ATTORNEY: Why did you keep looking at it?

607
00:42:14,300 --> 00:42:19,500
WITNESS B: I don't really know. I was waiting on my sister, so I was looking

608
00:42:19,500 --> 00:42:25,340
WITNESS B: up the road anyway for her car. She'd be coming from that direction, from

609
00:42:25,340 --> 00:42:29,820
WITNESS B: the west. So I was watching the cars come over the hill.

610
00:42:29,820 --> 00:42:34,990
ATTORNEY: So you were looking for your sister's car coming from the west?

611
00:42:34,990 --> 00:42:40,008
WITNESS B: Right. She drives a light-colored car, so when I saw a dark

612
00:42:40,008 --> 00:42:44,600
WITNESS B: one I knew it wasn't her, but I just kept watching it.

613
00:42:44,600 --> 00:42:50,510
ATTORNEY: About how long did you watch that dark car before it reached the intersection?

614
00:42:50,510 --> 00:42:54,950
WITNESS B: Not long. A few seconds. It was going pretty good.

615
00:42:54,950 --> 00:43:01,230
ATTORNEY: When you say a few seconds, can you give me any better estimate than that?

616
00:43:01,230 --> 00:43:05,415
WITNESS B: No. I wasn't counting. It wasn't a long time. It

617
00:43:05,415 --> 00:43:08,990
WITNESS B: came down the hill and then it was there.

618
00:43:08,990 --> 00:43:13,509
ATTORNEY: Let's talk about speed. Do you have an estimate of how

619
00:43:13,509 --> 00:43:17,860
ATTORNEY: fast the car was traveling as it came down the hill?

620
00:43:17,860 --> 00:43:19,330
OPPOSING COUNSEL: Objection. Foundation.

621
00:43:19,330 --> 00:43:23,030
ATTORNEY: You can answer if you have an estimate.

622
00:43:23,030 --> 00:43:28,570
WITNESS B: It was fast. Highway speed. It wasn't slowing down that I could tell.

623
00:43:28,570 --> 00:43:33,380
ATTORNEY: When you say highway speed, what do you mean by that?

624
00:43:33,380 --> 00:43:39,354
WITNESS B: I mean like the other cars that go through there. People go fast on that

625
00:43:39,354 --> 00:43:44,830
WITNESS B: road. It's a highway. It was going like a car on the highway goes.

626
00:43:44,830 --> 00:43:48,160
