01:01:33,220 --> 01:01:37,680
WITNESS B: A couple, I think. Not a lot. It wasn't busy.

888
01:01:37,680 --> 01:01:43,250
ATTORNEY: Tell me what you remember about the truck itself. Start with the trailer.

889
01:01:43,250 --> 01:01:47,174
WITNESS B: The trailer was white. Long. A box trailer, all

890
01:01:47,174 --> 01:01:50,680
WITNESS B: closed in. Like a big metal box on wheels.

891
01:01:50,680 --> 01:01:55,130
ATTORNEY: Did you notice anything on the front of the trailer?

892
01:01:55,130 --> 01:01:59,652
WITNESS B: There was a unit up on the front of it, up high, behind

893
01:01:59,652 --> 01:02:05,160
WITNESS B: the cab. A refrigeration thing, I'd guess. I could hear it running.

894
01:02:05,160 --> 01:02:07,760
ATTORNEY: What did it sound like?

895
01:02:07,760 --> 01:02:10,819
WITNESS B: A hum. Kind of a steady hum, like a

896
01:02:10,819 --> 01:02:15,190
WITNESS B: big air conditioner. You hear them at truck stops.

897
01:02:15,190 --> 01:02:20,390
ATTORNEY: Could you hear that hum from where you were outside the store?

898
01:02:20,390 --> 01:02:22,250
OPPOSING COUNSEL: Object to form.

899
01:02:22,250 --> 01:02:24,100
ATTORNEY: You can answer.

900
01:02:24,100 --> 01:02:30,420
WITNESS B: Yes. Once things got quiet between cars, you could hear it. It's a constant sound.

901
01:02:30,420 --> 01:02:35,990
ATTORNEY: What about the cab, the tractor part. What do you remember about that?

902
01:02:35,990 --> 01:02:42,018
WITNESS B: It was darker than the trailer. I don't remember the exact color. A regular

903
01:02:42,018 --> 01:02:46,760
WITNESS B: big rig cab. Not one of the flat-front ones, it had a hood.

904
01:02:46,760 --> 01:02:51,590
ATTORNEY: Do you have any estimate of how long the trailer was?

905
01:02:51,590 --> 01:02:55,719
WITNESS B: Long. The regular long kind. I couldn't give you feet.

906
01:02:55,719 --> 01:02:59,390
WITNESS B: I'm not good with distances, I said that before.

907
01:02:59,390 --> 01:03:03,067
ATTORNEY: That's fine. Would you say it was the size of

908
01:03:03,067 --> 01:03:07,560
ATTORNEY: trailer you typically see on the highway, the big ones?

909
01:03:07,560 --> 01:03:09,790
OPPOSING COUNSEL: Object to form. Leading.

910
01:03:09,790 --> 01:03:14,610
WITNESS B: Yes, the big ones. Not a short one. The full size.

911
01:03:14,610 --> 01:03:18,353
ATTORNEY: When you first noticed the truck in the turn

912
01:03:18,353 --> 01:03:21,670
ATTORNEY: lane, was it stopped, or was it moving?

913
01:03:21,670 --> 01:03:24,643
WITNESS B: I really can't tell you for sure. It was

914
01:03:24,643 --> 01:03:28,730
WITNESS B: either stopped or just barely rolling. Creeping, maybe.

915
01:03:28,730 --> 01:03:32,810
ATTORNEY: What makes you say it might have been creeping?

916
01:03:32,810 --> 01:03:38,780
WITNESS B: It just didn't seem totally still to me. But I wasn't staring at it. It

917
01:03:38,780 --> 01:03:44,330
WITNESS B: could have been stopped. I don't want to say one way or the other.

918
01:03:44,330 --> 01:03:48,538
ATTORNEY: I understand. I don't want you to guess. Is it fair

919
01:03:48,538 --> 01:03:53,240
ATTORNEY: to say you don't know whether it was stopped or creeping?

920
01:03:53,240 --> 01:03:59,180
WITNESS B: That's fair. It was one or the other. Sitting there or close to it.

921
01:03:59,180 --> 01:04:05,870
ATTORNEY: Do you know how long it was in the turn lane before it began its turn?

922
01:04:05,870 --> 01:04:09,348
WITNESS B: No. It was there when I noticed it. I

923
01:04:09,348 --> 01:04:12,920
WITNESS B: don't know how long it had been there.

924
01:04:12,920 --> 01:04:19,610
ATTORNEY: Were there any other vehicles in that turn lane, in front of it or behind it?

925
01:04:19,610 --> 01:04:22,950
WITNESS B: Not that I remember. Just the truck.

926
01:04:22,950 --> 01:04:27,410
ATTORNEY: Okay. At some point did the truck begin to turn?

927
01:04:27,410 --> 01:04:28,520
WITNESS B: Yes.

928
01:04:28,520 --> 01:04:32,240
ATTORNEY: Describe for me what you saw it do.

929
01:04:32,240 --> 01:04:36,724
WITNESS B: It started coming across. It pulled out of the turn lane, into

930
01:04:36,724 --> 01:04:40,990
WITNESS B: the crossover, the gap in the median, and then the front of

931
01:04:40,990 --> 01:04:45,980
WITNESS B: it started across the eastbound lanes. Toward our side. Toward 140th.

932
01:04:45,980 --> 01:04:50,104
ATTORNEY: When you say our side, you mean the south side

933
01:04:50,104 --> 01:04:53,780
ATTORNEY: of the highway, the side the store is on?

934
01:04:53,780 --> 01:04:56,010
WITNESS B: Yes. The store side.

935
01:04:56,010 --> 01:04:59,720
ATTORNEY: Which part of the truck came across first?

936
01:04:59,720 --> 01:05:04,143
WITNESS B: The cab. The front. Then the trailer follows behind it,

937
01:05:04,143 --> 01:05:07,520
WITNESS B: the way they do. It kind of swings around.

938
01:05:07,520 --> 01:05:11,980
ATTORNEY: Describe the path of the cab, as best you can.

939
01:05:11,980 --> 01:05:16,718
WITNESS B: It came out of the median and angled across, toward the side

940
01:05:16,718 --> 01:05:21,693
WITNESS B: road. Heading for 140th. It was turning left, so it was curving

941
01:05:21,693 --> 01:05:25,720
WITNESS B: toward my left as I looked at it. Toward the south.

942
01:05:25,720 --> 01:05:27,580
OPPOSING COUNSEL: Object to form.

943
01:05:27,580 --> 01:05:31,532
ATTORNEY: I'll rephrase. From where you were, which way did

944
01:05:31,532 --> 01:05:35,000
ATTORNEY: the cab appear to be heading as it crossed?

945
01:05:35,000 --> 01:05:40,200
WITNESS B: Toward 140th. Toward the side road that goes down past the store.

946
01:05:40,200 --> 01:05:46,150
ATTORNEY: Did it appear to you to be making a normal left turn into 140th?

947
01:05:46,150 --> 01:05:48,380
OPPOSING COUNSEL: Object to form. Foundation.

948
01:05:48,380 --> 01:05:50,600
ATTORNEY: If you can answer.

949
01:05:50,600 --> 01:05:54,757
WITNESS B: It looked like a regular left turn to me. It was

950
01:05:54,757 --> 01:05:59,520
WITNESS B: going where the road goes. I'm not an expert in trucks.

951
01:05:59,520 --> 01:06:03,600
ATTORNEY: How fast was the truck moving as it turned?

952
01:06:03,600 --> 01:06:04,720
WITNESS B: Slow.

953
01:06:04,720 --> 01:06:08,800
ATTORNEY: Can you give me any sense of how slow?

954
01:06:08,800 --> 01:06:10,660
OPPOSING COUNSEL: Object to form.

955
01:06:10,660 --> 01:06:15,561
WITNESS B: Slow like a big truck turning. A little faster than somebody walking,

956
01:06:15,561 --> 01:06:20,320
WITNESS B: maybe. Not much. They don't go fast when they're turning like that.

957
01:06:20,320 --> 01:06:24,770
ATTORNEY: Did the speed change as it went through the turn?

958
01:06:24,770 --> 01:06:30,404
WITNESS B: Not that I could tell. It was kind of steady. Slow and steady. Maybe

959
01:06:30,404 --> 01:06:35,540
WITNESS B: it picked up a little once it was moving. I really don't know.

960
01:06:35,540 --> 01:06:41,490
ATTORNEY: Did you see it stop at any point during the turn, before the crash?

961
01:06:41,490 --> 01:06:47,060
WITNESS B: No. I didn't see it stop. Once it started across, it kept going.

962
01:06:47,060 --> 01:06:53,740
ATTORNEY: How long, from when it started moving out of the turn lane, did the turn take?

963
01:06:53,740 --> 01:06:55,600
OPPOSING COUNSEL: Object to form.

964
01:06:55,600 --> 01:06:59,390
WITNESS B: A few seconds. I don't know. It felt slow. It

965
01:06:59,390 --> 01:07:03,770
WITNESS B: wasn't like a car whipping across. It took its time.

966
01:07:03,770 --> 01:07:10,080
ATTORNEY: When you say a few seconds, are you able to put any number on that?

967
01:07:10,080 --> 01:07:13,963
WITNESS B: No. I'd be making it up. Several seconds. It

968
01:07:13,963 --> 01:07:17,140
WITNESS B: was slow. That's all I can tell you.

969
01:07:17,140 --> 01:07:23,830
ATTORNEY: I'm not asking you to make anything up. If you don't know, that's a fine answer.

970
01:07:23,830 --> 01:07:30,510
WITNESS B: Then I don't know the exact number. It was a few seconds, and it was slow.

971
01:07:30,510 --> 01:07:34,970
ATTORNEY: As the truck turned, did you hear anything from it?

972
01:07:34,970 --> 01:07:39,425
WITNESS B: The engine. You could hear the engine working, like a low

973
01:07:39,425 --> 01:07:43,880
WITNESS B: rumble when they pull out. And that hum from the trailer.

974
01:07:43,880 --> 01:07:47,600
ATTORNEY: Did the engine noise change during the turn?

975
01:07:47,600 --> 01:07:51,937
WITNESS B: It got a little louder when it started pulling. Then it

976
01:07:51,937 --> 01:07:56,510
WITNESS B: was just steady. Like a big diesel. That's all I remember.

977
01:07:56,510 --> 01:08:00,590
ATTORNEY: Did you hear the truck's horn at any point?

978
01:08:00,590 --> 01:08:03,570
WITNESS B: No. I don't remember any horn.

979
01:08:03,570 --> 01:08:08,020
ATTORNEY: Did you hear any air brakes, that hiss trucks make?

980
01:08:08,020 --> 01:08:13,220
WITNESS B: No. I didn't hear brakes. Not from the truck, not from anybody.

981
01:08:13,220 --> 01:08:19,160
ATTORNEY: Did you hear any other sounds from the truck, any squeal, anything like that?

982
01:08:19,160 --> 01:08:22,510
WITNESS B: No. Just the engine and the hum.

983
01:08:22,510 --> 01:08:26,960
ATTORNEY: Did you notice whether the truck had any lights on?

984
01:08:26,960 --> 01:08:32,530
WITNESS B: I didn't notice lights. It was broad daylight. I wasn't looking for that.

985
01:08:32,530 --> 01:08:36,620
ATTORNEY: Did you notice a turn signal on the truck?

986
01:08:36,620 --> 01:08:40,703
WITNESS B: I don't remember. I didn't notice it either way.

987
01:08:40,703 --> 01:08:43,680
WITNESS B: I'm not saying it was or wasn't on.

988
01:08:43,680 --> 01:08:48,085
ATTORNEY: Understood. Now, as the truck came across the eastbound lanes,

989
01:08:48,085 --> 01:08:51,850
ATTORNEY: where did the trailer end up relative to those lanes?

990
01:08:51,850 --> 01:08:57,050
WITNESS B: Across them. The trailer was stretched across the road. Both eastbound lanes.

991
01:08:57,050 --> 01:08:58,530
ATTORNEY: Both lanes?

992
01:08:58,530 --> 01:09:02,884
WITNESS B: Both. The inside lane and the outside lane. It was long

993
01:09:02,884 --> 01:09:07,080
WITNESS B: enough that it covered the whole thing, more or less.

994
01:09:07,080 --> 01:09:10,967
ATTORNEY: When you say covered, do you mean the trailer was

995
01:09:10,967 --> 01:09:15,250
ATTORNEY: across both of the eastbound lanes at the same moment?

996
01:09:15,250 --> 01:09:19,955
WITNESS B: Yes. At one point it was across both of them. The cab was

997
01:09:19,955 --> 01:09:25,650
WITNESS B: over toward 140th and the trailer was back across the road behind it.

998
01:09:25,650 --> 01:09:27,500
OPPOSING COUNSEL: Object to form.

999
01:09:27,500 --> 01:09:30,885
ATTORNEY: Let me break that down. At the moment the

1000
01:09:30,885 --> 01:09:34,930
ATTORNEY: trailer was across both lanes, where was the cab?

1001
01:09:34,930 --> 01:09:39,741
WITNESS B: The cab was mostly across already. Up near the edge of the

1002
01:09:39,741 --> 01:09:44,220
WITNESS B: road on our side, starting into 140th, or close to it.

1003
01:09:44,220 --> 01:09:48,300
ATTORNEY: And the back of the trailer, where was that?

1004
01:09:48,300 --> 01:09:52,689
WITNESS B: Still back in the median area, I think. Back toward where it

1005
01:09:52,689 --> 01:09:57,590
WITNESS B: came from. The back wheels were still coming through the crossover.

1006
01:09:57,590 --> 01:10:02,410
ATTORNEY: Are you confident about where the back of the trailer was?

1007
01:10:02,410 --> 01:10:07,282
WITNESS B: Not exactly confident. It was back there somewhere. In the median

1008
01:10:07,282 --> 01:10:11,330
WITNESS B: or right near it. I wasn't looking at the back wheels.

1009
01:10:11,330 --> 01:10:16,900
ATTORNEY: Okay. Was the trailer moving or stopped when it was across both lanes?

1010
01:10:16,900 --> 01:10:20,610
WITNESS B: Moving. Slow, still moving. It was still turning.

1011
01:10:20,610 --> 01:10:25,440
ATTORNEY: Was the trailer straight across the road, or at an angle?

1012
01:10:25,440 --> 01:10:27,300
OPPOSING COUNSEL: Object to form.

1013
01:10:27,300 --> 01:10:31,608
WITNESS B: At an angle, I'd say. Because it was still bending around

1014
01:10:31,608 --> 01:10:35,840
WITNESS B: the turn. Not straight across like a wall, more slanted.

1015
01:10:35,840 --> 01:10:39,550
ATTORNEY: Slanted in which direction, if you can say?

1016
01:10:39,550 --> 01:10:44,029
WITNESS B: I can't really say better than that. It was angled. The

1017
01:10:44,029 --> 01:10:48,100
WITNESS B: front was ahead of the back. That's how they turn.

1018
01:10:48,100 --> 01:10:53,670
ATTORNEY: Fair enough. Which side of the trailer was facing the oncoming eastbound traffic?

1019
01:10:53,670 --> 01:10:55,900
OPPOSING COUNSEL: Object to form. Foundation.

1020
01:10:55,900 --> 01:10:57,750
ATTORNEY: If you know.

1021
01:10:57,750 --> 01:11:03,720
WITNESS B: The side of it. The long side. Coming from the west you'd be looking at

1022
01:11:03,720 --> 01:11:09,270
WITNESS B: the long side. The right side of it, I guess, if you're the truck.

1023
01:11:09,270 --> 01:11:13,089
ATTORNEY: Okay. Let me go back a step. When the truck

1024
01:11:13,089 --> 01:11:17,440
ATTORNEY: started its turn, where was the car, if you know?

1025
01:11:17,440 --> 01:11:19,290
OPPOSING COUNSEL: Object to form.

1026
01:11:19,290 --> 01:11:23,418
WITNESS B: Coming down the hill. Coming east. It had already come

1027
01:11:23,418 --> 01:11:27,470
WITNESS B: over the top, I think, when the truck started moving.

1028
01:11:27,470 --> 01:11:30,060
ATTORNEY: You think, or you know?

1029
01:11:30,060 --> 01:11:35,396
WITNESS B: I think. I believe the car was already over the hill when the truck

1030
01:11:35,396 --> 01:11:41,210
WITNESS B: pulled out. That's how I remember it. But I wouldn't swear to the second.

1031
01:11:41,210 --> 01:11:47,425
ATTORNEY: In your earlier testimony this morning you said you first noticed the car as it

1032
01:11:47,425 --> 01:11:53,090
ATTORNEY: came over the hill. Was the truck still in the turn lane at that moment?

1033
01:11:53,090 --> 01:11:57,598
WITNESS B: I think it was still in the turn lane, or just starting.

1034
01:11:57,598 --> 01:12:02,750
WITNESS B: It started across after, or about the same time. Not long after.

1035
01:12:02,750 --> 01:12:07,430
ATTORNEY: So the sequence you recall is the car comes over the hill,

1036
01:12:07,430 --> 01:12:12,030
ATTORNEY: and then the truck begins across, or about the same time?

1037
01:12:12,030 --> 01:12:15,000
OPPOSING COUNSEL: Object to form. Asked and answered.

1038
01:12:15,000 --> 01:12:16,860
ATTORNEY: You can answer.

1039
01:12:16,860 --> 01:12:23,550
