ATTORNEY: Did you see any damage to the trailer from where you were?

1245
01:26:42,390 --> 01:26:48,756
WITNESS B: I saw it later, when it was stopped. The side was messed up. There was a

1246
01:26:48,756 --> 01:26:55,210
WITNESS B: big dent, kind of torn along the bottom edge. I didn't go up close to it.

1247
01:26:55,210 --> 01:26:58,600
ATTORNEY: Which side of the trailer was damaged?

1248
01:26:58,600 --> 01:27:04,029
WITNESS B: The side that had been facing the car. After it turned, that side

1249
01:27:04,029 --> 01:27:08,790
WITNESS B: was facing kind of west, toward the road. I could see it.

1250
01:27:08,790 --> 01:27:15,159
ATTORNEY: I'm not going to ask you about any person. I just want to understand where you

1251
01:27:15,159 --> 01:27:21,610
ATTORNEY: were and what you did. Immediately after the car hit the pole, what did you do?

1252
01:27:21,610 --> 01:27:26,744
WITNESS B: I just stood there. I couldn't move for a second. I think I

1253
01:27:26,744 --> 01:27:31,790
WITNESS B: said something out loud, like oh my God. I dropped my bag.

1254
01:27:31,790 --> 01:27:34,810
ATTORNEY: The shopping bag you mentioned earlier?

1255
01:27:34,810 --> 01:27:41,600
WITNESS B: Yes. Stuff went all over. I didn't even care. I left it there for a while.

1256
01:27:41,600 --> 01:27:45,370
ATTORNEY: Did you move from where you were standing?

1257
01:27:45,370 --> 01:27:49,576
WITNESS B: Not much. I stayed out front of the store. I took

1258
01:27:49,576 --> 01:27:54,040
WITNESS B: a couple steps, toward the road, and then I stopped.

1259
01:27:54,040 --> 01:27:56,300
ATTORNEY: Why did you stop?

1260
01:27:56,300 --> 01:28:00,924
WITNESS B: Because I didn't know what to do. There were cars still

1261
01:28:00,924 --> 01:28:05,548
WITNESS B: coming on the highway, I didn't want to walk out there.

1262
01:28:05,548 --> 01:28:09,500
WITNESS B: And it was so far down there where the car was.

1263
01:28:09,500 --> 01:28:14,780
ATTORNEY: Did you ever walk down to where the car came to rest?

1264
01:28:14,780 --> 01:28:21,570
WITNESS B: No. I didn't go down there. I didn't want to see. I'll be honest about that.

1265
01:28:21,570 --> 01:28:26,642
ATTORNEY: That's fine. Nobody is going to ask you to describe anything you

1266
01:28:26,642 --> 01:28:31,000
ATTORNEY: didn't see. Did anyone else go down there that you saw?

1267
01:28:31,000 --> 01:28:35,687
WITNESS B: Some people stopped their cars on the highway and ran down

1268
01:28:35,687 --> 01:28:40,050
WITNESS B: there. A couple of people. I don't know who they were.

1269
01:28:40,050 --> 01:28:43,820
ATTORNEY: About how many vehicles stopped, if you remember?

1270
01:28:43,820 --> 01:28:50,610
WITNESS B: Two or three at first. Then more. After a while there were cars pulled off everywhere.

1271
01:28:50,610 --> 01:28:54,760
ATTORNEY: Did you make a phone call at some point?

1272
01:28:54,760 --> 01:28:57,400
WITNESS B: Yes. I called my sister.

1273
01:28:57,400 --> 01:29:01,550
ATTORNEY: How soon after the crash did you call her?

1274
01:29:01,550 --> 01:29:06,830
WITNESS B: A few minutes. Maybe a minute or two. I had to find my

1275
01:29:06,830 --> 01:29:12,110
WITNESS B: phone, it was in my bag and the bag was on the ground.

1276
01:29:12,110 --> 01:29:14,370
ATTORNEY: Did you call 911?

1277
01:29:14,370 --> 01:29:19,586
WITNESS B: No. I thought about it, but somebody said they already called. And

1278
01:29:19,586 --> 01:29:24,170
WITNESS B: then the lady from the store came out and said she called.

1279
01:29:24,170 --> 01:29:27,940
ATTORNEY: Who said they already called, the first time?

1280
01:29:27,940 --> 01:29:29,450
OPPOSING COUNSEL: Object. Hearsay.

1281
01:29:29,450 --> 01:29:35,860
ATTORNEY: I'm not asking for the truth of it. Just who said it, if you know.

1282
01:29:35,860 --> 01:29:39,492
WITNESS B: One of the people who stopped. A man, I

1283
01:29:39,492 --> 01:29:43,030
WITNESS B: think. He yelled it. I don't know him.

1284
01:29:43,030 --> 01:29:47,550
ATTORNEY: What did you say to your sister on the phone?

1285
01:29:47,550 --> 01:29:49,060
OPPOSING COUNSEL: Object. Hearsay.

1286
01:29:49,060 --> 01:29:50,950
ATTORNEY: You can answer.

1287
01:29:50,950 --> 01:29:55,240
WITNESS B: I told her there was a terrible wreck right in front

1288
01:29:55,240 --> 01:29:59,282
WITNESS B: of the store and to hurry up, and that she should

1289
01:29:59,282 --> 01:30:04,150
WITNESS B: be careful coming because the road was going to be blocked.

1290
01:30:04,150 --> 01:30:06,410
ATTORNEY: What did she say?

1291
01:30:06,410 --> 01:30:07,920
OPPOSING COUNSEL: Same objection.

1292
01:30:07,920 --> 01:30:12,887
WITNESS B: She said she was close and she was coming. That's about

1293
01:30:12,887 --> 01:30:16,590
WITNESS B: it. I was crying, so it was hard to talk.

1294
01:30:16,590 --> 01:30:23,380
ATTORNEY: Let's talk about the store employee. At some point did someone come out of the store?

1295
01:30:23,380 --> 01:30:28,280
WITNESS B: Yes. The woman who worked the counter. She came running out.

1296
01:30:28,280 --> 01:30:32,430
ATTORNEY: How soon after the crash did she come out?

1297
01:30:32,430 --> 01:30:38,890
WITNESS B: Pretty fast. Right after. Maybe while I was still standing there. Before I called my

1298
01:30:38,890 --> 01:30:44,120
WITNESS B: sister, I think. Or around the same time. I'm not sure of the order.

1299
01:30:44,120 --> 01:30:48,270
ATTORNEY: When she came out, did you talk with her?

1300
01:30:48,270 --> 01:30:49,400
WITNESS B: Yes.

1301
01:30:49,400 --> 01:30:52,800
ATTORNEY: Tell me what you said to her.

1302
01:30:52,800 --> 01:30:54,310
OPPOSING COUNSEL: Object. Hearsay.

1303
01:30:54,310 --> 01:30:58,080
ATTORNEY: These are her own statements. You can answer.

1304
01:30:58,080 --> 01:31:01,962
WITNESS B: I told her a car went under the truck. I told

1305
01:31:01,962 --> 01:31:05,931
WITNESS B: her it went way down there and hit the pole. I

1306
01:31:05,931 --> 01:31:11,280
WITNESS B: was pointing. I was pretty upset. I don't remember every word.

1307
01:31:11,280 --> 01:31:14,290
ATTORNEY: Did she ask you any questions?

1308
01:31:14,290 --> 01:31:17,853
WITNESS B: She asked me what happened. She asked if I

1309
01:31:17,853 --> 01:31:21,840
WITNESS B: was okay. She asked if anybody called for help.

1310
01:31:21,840 --> 01:31:24,480
ATTORNEY: Did she stay with you?

1311
01:31:24,480 --> 01:31:29,005
WITNESS B: For a little while. Then she went back in and out

1312
01:31:29,005 --> 01:31:33,530
WITNESS B: a couple of times. She was on the phone, I think.

1313
01:31:33,530 --> 01:31:38,050
ATTORNEY: Did you tell her anything else about what you saw?

1314
01:31:38,050 --> 01:31:39,940
OPPOSING COUNSEL: Object to form.

1315
01:31:39,940 --> 01:31:45,145
WITNESS B: Probably. I was talking a lot. I kept saying it over and

1316
01:31:45,145 --> 01:31:49,792
WITNESS B: over. I think I said I saw the whole thing. I know

1317
01:31:49,792 --> 01:31:53,510
WITNESS B: I said that to a lot of people that day.

1318
01:31:53,510 --> 01:31:58,790
ATTORNEY: Do you remember anything she said to you, other than the questions?

1319
01:31:58,790 --> 01:31:59,920
OPPOSING COUNSEL: Hearsay.

1320
01:31:59,920 --> 01:32:04,483
WITNESS B: She said something like she didn't see it, she just heard it

1321
01:32:04,483 --> 01:32:09,350
WITNESS B: from inside. She said it shook the windows. Something like that.

1322
01:32:09,350 --> 01:32:14,260
ATTORNEY: Did the two of you talk about where you were standing?

1323
01:32:14,260 --> 01:32:16,140
OPPOSING COUNSEL: Object to form.

1324
01:32:16,140 --> 01:32:20,330
WITNESS B: I don't remember that. I don't think we talked about

1325
01:32:20,330 --> 01:32:24,440
WITNESS B: it like that. We were just talking about the wreck.

1326
01:32:24,440 --> 01:32:28,590
ATTORNEY: All right. Did any police or emergency vehicles arrive?

1327
01:32:28,590 --> 01:32:35,370
WITNESS B: Yes. Deputies came. And an ambulance, and the fire truck, I think. A bunch of them.

1328
01:32:35,370 --> 01:32:39,900
ATTORNEY: How long after the crash did the first one arrive?

1329
01:32:39,900 --> 01:32:41,790
OPPOSING COUNSEL: Object to form.

1330
01:32:41,790 --> 01:32:48,570
WITNESS B: It felt like forever. But it was probably ten minutes. Maybe less. I really don't know.

1331
01:32:48,570 --> 01:32:52,340
ATTORNEY: Did any of them stop at the intersection?

1332
01:32:52,340 --> 01:32:56,333
WITNESS B: Later, yes. A deputy car parked up by the crossover

1333
01:32:56,333 --> 01:33:00,640
WITNESS B: with the lights on. And they started blocking the road.

1334
01:33:00,640 --> 01:33:03,280
ATTORNEY: Did they close the highway?

1335
01:33:03,280 --> 01:33:07,838
WITNESS B: The eastbound side, at least. They were waving people around.

1336
01:33:07,838 --> 01:33:11,200
WITNESS B: It was a while before cars could get through.

1337
01:33:11,200 --> 01:33:15,350
ATTORNEY: Was your sister able to get to the store?

1338
01:33:15,350 --> 01:33:21,104
WITNESS B: Yes. She got there around five. She had to come around a different way,

1339
01:33:21,104 --> 01:33:26,290
WITNESS B: I think, or they let her through. She pulled into the store lot.

1340
01:33:26,290 --> 01:33:29,680
ATTORNEY: Did you leave when your sister arrived?

1341
01:33:29,680 --> 01:33:33,341
WITNESS B: No. Not right away. I wanted to tell somebody

1342
01:33:33,341 --> 01:33:36,840
WITNESS B: what I saw. I thought somebody should know.

1343
01:33:36,840 --> 01:33:40,620
ATTORNEY: Did you speak to a deputy that day?

1344
01:33:40,620 --> 01:33:47,400
WITNESS B: Yes. One of them came up to the store. He was asking if anybody saw it.

1345
01:33:47,400 --> 01:33:50,040
ATTORNEY: What did you tell him?

1346
01:33:50,040 --> 01:33:51,550
OPPOSING COUNSEL: Object. Hearsay.

1347
01:33:51,550 --> 01:33:53,440
ATTORNEY: You can answer.

1348
01:33:53,440 --> 01:33:57,085
WITNESS B: I told him I saw it. I told him I saw

1349
01:33:57,085 --> 01:34:02,010
WITNESS B: the car come down the hill and go under the truck.

1350
01:34:02,010 --> 01:34:06,640
WITNESS B: I told him it went down there and hit the pole.

1351
01:34:06,640 --> 01:34:09,650
ATTORNEY: Did the deputy write anything down?

1352
01:34:09,650 --> 01:34:13,908
WITNESS B: He wrote some things in a little notebook. He took

1353
01:34:13,908 --> 01:34:17,570
WITNESS B: my name and my phone number and my address.

1354
01:34:17,570 --> 01:34:22,480
ATTORNEY: Did he ask you to give a written statement that day?

1355
01:34:22,480 --> 01:34:28,781
WITNESS B: No, not that day. He said somebody would contact me. And then a few days later

1356
01:34:28,781 --> 01:34:34,920
WITNESS B: they did, and I wrote it out. That's the statement I looked at before today.

1357
01:34:34,920 --> 01:34:39,179
ATTORNEY: We'll talk about that statement in more detail later. How

1358
01:34:39,179 --> 01:34:42,840
ATTORNEY: long did you talk with the deputy that afternoon?

1359
01:34:42,840 --> 01:34:48,500
WITNESS B: Not long. Five minutes. He was busy. There were a lot of people.

1360
01:34:48,500 --> 01:34:53,020
ATTORNEY: Did he ask you where you were when it happened?

1361
01:34:53,020 --> 01:34:54,910
OPPOSING COUNSEL: Object to form.

1362
01:34:54,910 --> 01:34:59,387
WITNESS B: He asked if I was there. I said I was out front

1363
01:34:59,387 --> 01:35:04,340
WITNESS B: of the store. I don't think he asked more than that.

1364
01:35:04,340 --> 01:35:09,620
ATTORNEY: Did he show you anything, a diagram, a photo, anything like that?

1365
01:35:09,620 --> 01:35:11,880
WITNESS B: No. Nothing like that.

1366
01:35:11,880 --> 01:35:16,030
ATTORNEY: Did any other official talk with you that day?

1367
01:35:16,030 --> 01:35:19,800
WITNESS B: Not that I remember. Just the one deputy.

1368
01:35:19,800 --> 01:35:24,700
ATTORNEY: Did you see the truck get moved while you were there?

1369
01:35:24,700 --> 01:35:29,600
WITNESS B: No. It was still sitting down on 140th when we left.

1370
01:35:29,600 --> 01:35:32,620
ATTORNEY: About what time did you leave?

1371
01:35:32,620 --> 01:35:37,520
WITNESS B: Maybe five thirty. Quarter to six. It was still light out.

1372
01:35:37,520 --> 01:35:42,430
ATTORNEY: Did anyone tell you anything about the people in the car?

1373
01:35:42,430 --> 01:35:44,690
OPPOSING COUNSEL: Object. Calls for hearsay.

1374
01:35:44,690 --> 01:35:49,358
ATTORNEY: I'll withdraw that. Let me ask it differently. Did you yourself

1375
01:35:49,358 --> 01:35:53,360
ATTORNEY: see anything about the condition of anyone in the car?

1376
01:35:53,360 --> 01:35:57,012
WITNESS B: No. I didn't go down there, and I didn't see

1377
01:35:57,012 --> 01:36:01,660
WITNESS B: anything like that. I'd rather not talk about that part.

1378
01:36:01,660 --> 01:36:07,261
ATTORNEY: That's fine. I'm not going to ask you about that. Let me go back to

1379
01:36:07,261 --> 01:36:12,862
ATTORNEY: a couple of things. You said the car went off the south side of the

1380
01:36:12,862 --> 01:36:18,630
ATTORNEY: road. Do you know about where along the highway it left the pavement?

1381
01:36:18,630 --> 01:36:20,520
OPPOSING COUNSEL: Object to form.

1382
01:36:20,520 --> 01:36:25,800
WITNESS B: Not exactly. A ways past the intersection. Past the store. Further down.

1383
01:36:25,800 --> 01:36:28,810
ATTORNEY: Past the store to the east?

1384
01:36:28,810 --> 01:36:30,320
WITNESS B: Yes, east.

1385
01:36:30,320 --> 01:36:33,960
ATTORNEY: Did you see where the car went relative to

1386
01:36:33,960 --> 01:36:37,860
ATTORNEY: the store itself? Did it come near the store?

1387
01:36:37,860 --> 01:36:42,867
WITNESS B: No, it didn't come near the store. It was out on the road

1388
01:36:42,867 --> 01:36:48,050
WITNESS B: and then off past it, down the shoulder and into the field.

1389
01:36:48,050 --> 01:36:52,630
ATTORNEY: Was there any other vehicle on the eastbound side of the

1390
01:36:52,630 --> 01:36:56,720
ATTORNEY: highway at the moment of the impact, that you saw?

1391
01:36:56,720 --> 01:36:58,600
OPPOSING COUNSEL: Object to form.

1392
01:36:58,600 --> 01:37:04,260
WITNESS B: No. Not right there. There was nobody else right there that I remember.

1393
01:37:04,260 --> 01:37:07,280
ATTORNEY: What about on the westbound side?

1394
01:37:07,280 --> 01:37:14,070
WITNESS B: I don't remember anything on the westbound side right then. Maybe something further off. Nothing close.

1395
01:37:14,070 --> 01:37:18,970
ATTORNEY: After the impact, did any eastbound cars come over the hill?

1396
01:37:18,970 --> 01:37:24,481
WITNESS B: Yes. A minute or so after, I think, a car came over and slowed way

1397
01:37:24,481 --> 01:37:30,660
WITNESS B: down. Then pulled over. That might have been one of the ones that stopped.

1398
01:37:30,660 --> 01:37:35,940
ATTORNEY: Did any vehicle have to go around the truck on the highway?

1399
01:37:35,940 --> 01:37:40,534
WITNESS B: No, by then the truck was already off the highway. It was

1400
01:37:40,534 --> 01:37:45,370
WITNESS B: down 140th. The road was clear except for, you know, pieces.

1401
01:37:45,370 --> 01:37:47,250
ATTORNEY: Pieces of what?

1402
01:37:47,250 --> 01:37:51,066
WITNESS B: Debris. Glass and parts. There was stuff on the

1403
01:37:51,066 --> 01:37:54,800
WITNESS B: road by the crossover. I could see it shining.

1404
01:37:54,800 --> 01:37:59,320
ATTORNEY: Did you touch or pick up any of that debris?

1405
01:37:59,320 --> 01:38:03,090
WITNESS B: No. I didn't go out on the road.

1406
01:38:03,090 --> 01:38:09,500
ATTORNEY: At any point that afternoon, did you go out into the highway or the median?

1407
01:38:09,500 --> 01:38:13,650
WITNESS B: No. I stayed by the store the whole time.

1408
01:38:13,650 --> 01:38:19,690
ATTORNEY: When you say by the store, you mean out front, the area you've described?

1409
01:38:19,690 --> 01:38:23,460
WITNESS B: Yes. Out front. And inside that one time.

1410
01:38:23,460 --> 01:38:27,230
ATTORNEY: All right. Did your sister see the crash?

1411
01:38:27,230 --> 01:38:31,000
WITNESS B: No. She wasn't there yet. She came after.

1412
01:38:31,000 --> 01:38:35,900
ATTORNEY: When your sister arrived, did you tell her what you saw?

1413
01:38:35,900 --> 01:38:40,564
WITNESS B: Yes, I told her the whole thing in the car on the way

1414
01:38:40,564 --> 01:38:46,460
WITNESS B: home. I told her again later too. I couldn't stop talking about it.

1415
01:38:46,460 --> 01:38:49,860
ATTORNEY: How were you feeling physically that afternoon?

1416
01:38:49,860 --> 01:38:53,857
WITNESS B: Shaky. My legs were like jelly. I wasn't hurt. I

1417
01:38:53,857 --> 01:38:57,770
WITNESS B: was just upset. I didn't sleep good that night.

1418
01:38:57,770 --> 01:39:04,064
ATTORNEY: Thinking back on everything that happened after the impact, from the bang to the time

1419
01:39:04,064 --> 01:39:09,470
ATTORNEY: you left, is there anything you saw that you haven't told us about today?

1420
01:39:09,470 --> 01:39:11,350
OPPOSING COUNSEL: Object to form.

1421
01:39:11,350 --> 01:39:16,847
WITNESS B: I don't think so. I think I've told you all of it. The bang, the car

1422
01:39:16,847 --> 01:39:23,800
WITNESS B: going down there, the pole, the truck stopping. The lady from the store. The deputies.

1423
01:39:23,800 --> 01:39:29,080
ATTORNEY: Is there anything about what you heard that you haven't told us?

1424
01:39:29,080 --> 01:39:33,804
WITNESS B: Just that it was loud. Then after, it got real quiet for a

1425
01:39:33,804 --> 01:39:39,260
WITNESS B: little bit. Except the truck. That hum kept going. I remember that.

1426
01:39:39,260 --> 01:39:44,956
ATTORNEY: All right. I'm going to shift gears in a moment to your written statement

1427
01:39:44,956 --> 01:39:50,808
ATTORNEY: and some other things. Before I do, is there anything about your answers in

1428
01:39:50,808 --> 01:39:55,100
ATTORNEY: the last few minutes that you want to change or add to?

1429
01:39:55,100 --> 01:39:57,740
WITNESS B: No. That's what I remember.

1430
01:39:57,740 --> 01:40:00,000
ATTORNEY: Okay. Thank you. Let's keep going.

1431
01:40:00,000 --> 01:40:06,663
ATTORNEY: Let's keep going. I want to circle back to a few things from earlier before I

1432
01:40:06,663 --> 01:40:13,240
ATTORNEY: show you a document. Are you doing all right? Do you need water or anything?

1433
01:40:13,240 --> 01:40:16,850
WITNESS B: I'm fine. I have water. Thank you.

1434
01:40:16,850 --> 01:40:20,649
ATTORNEY: Earlier you told us your sister picked you up

1435
01:40:20,649 --> 01:40:24,870
ATTORNEY: that afternoon. About what time did she get there?

1436
01:40:24,870 --> 01:40:28,890
WITNESS B: Around five. Maybe a couple of minutes after.

1437
01:40:28,890 --> 01:40:36,110
ATTORNEY: So from the time of the collision until your sister arrived, about how long was that?

1438
01:40:36,110 --> 01:40:40,120
WITNESS B: Twenty-five minutes, something like that. It felt longer.

1439
01:40:40,120 --> 01:40:46,140
ATTORNEY: During those twenty-five minutes, did you stay at the store the entire time?

1440
01:40:46,140 --> 01:40:51,350
WITNESS B: Yes. I didn't leave the store property. I stayed out front.

1441
01:40:51,350 --> 01:40:57,370
ATTORNEY: Did you ever walk down the highway toward where the car ended up?

1442
01:40:57,370 --> 01:41:02,190
WITNESS B: No. I didn't go down there. I didn't want to.

1443
01:41:02,190 --> 01:41:07,000
ATTORNEY: Did you walk down Northeast 140th Court toward the truck?

1444
01:41:07,000 --> 01:41:10,610
WITNESS B: No. I stayed up by the store.

1445
01:41:10,610 --> 01:41:14,620
ATTORNEY: When your sister arrived, where did she park?

1446
01:41:14,620 --> 01:41:19,045
WITNESS B: In the little lot by the store. She couldn't get in

1447
01:41:19,045 --> 01:41:24,250
WITNESS B: easy because of all the deputies' cars, but she squeezed in.

1448
01:41:24,250 --> 01:41:27,860
ATTORNEY: Did you tell her what had happened?

1449
01:41:27,860 --> 01:41:32,476
